  "oracle_attribution": "The added/edited assertions in max_alloc and stats_check reference stats.max_footprint, a field absent from heapmem_stats_t at the base (confirmed in os/lib/heapmem.h lines 87-93, and compile_requirements lists max_footprint as at_base: false in os/lib/heapmem.h). The unit therefore cannot compile at the base. The missing interface is precisely the PR's purpose: adding a peak-usage field to the heap statistics. The production change adds max_footprint to the struct, tracks it in extend_space(), and reports it from heapmem_stats(), so the same tests compile and pass after the fix.",
